    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n80606" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πενθ-ῐκός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of</i> or <i>for mourning, mournful</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀδυρμοί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.102b
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θέα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Porph.
					<u>Abst.</u>
					2.50
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐσθής</span> Chor.<i><span class="en">
				p.6B.
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν πενθικοῖς</span> (sc.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐσθήμασι</span>) <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Ex.</u>
				33.4
			</span></i>. Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς, ἔχειν τινός</span> to be <i>in
				mourning</i> for a person, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				5.2.7
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάνυ π. ἐσκευασμένη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Cal.</u>
					5
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.1
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				13d
			</span></i> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ητικῶς</span>
			).</div>
